Subject: [PATCH] Give compositor and presentation fixtures the Vulkan test backend

These fixtures use the same Vulkan dispatch as VulkanTest. Without the bundled
loader and SwiftShader environment, Intel hosts can load an incompatible system
backend and crash before evaluating their feature requirements. Keep all Vulkan
fixtures in the existing isolated group; unrelated and Crashpad tests retain the
normal loader environment. Unsupported swapchain features keep upstream skips.

--- a/android/build/python/aemu/tasks/unit_tests.py
+++ b/android/build/python/aemu/tasks/unit_tests.py
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@
         # Loader-path overrides change dyld crash annotations. Restrict the
         # headless graphics fixture to Vulkan tests instead of affecting
         # Crashpad and the rest of the native test suite.
-        graphics = r"^(VulkanTest|VulkanFrameBufferTest)\."
+        graphics = r"^(VulkanTest|VulkanFrameBufferTest|CompositorVkTest|SwapChainStateVkTest|DisplayVkTest)\."
         graphics_env = dict(env)
         graphics_env.update({
             "DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH": ":".join(str(self.destination / path) for path in
